https://www.photoonmaps.com — display your photos on Google Earth.

Turn geotagged photos into a 3D map, save trips into own folder, and share them as links or Google Earth `.KMZ` files.


When browsering to site https://www.photoonmaps.com, one will see a demo/sample site,
which is a group of photos taken while hiking Mount Sanitas, Boulder, Colorado.

Click on each (red) pin, will have a thumbnail pop up showing the picture at that point.
Clikc on the thumbnail, a larger photo will pop-up in a new window.

To start import/upload your own photos.

1. click "Clear" button at top-right.
2. click the dashed rectecgular at left panel to upload your photos,
   or drag and drop your selected photo(s) to the dashed rectangular.
3. If your photos are geotagged, it will show a square with blue tick.
   on the right, there is a square with red cross, which allow you to remove it (if you do not want to share).
   
   If you photos are not geotagged, there will be a empty square at left on the imgage square,
   with red string under the image (small thumbnail).
   
   We can only use geotagged photos.
   
4. After you import all photos you want to share (usually for a trip, with 10-20 photos).

   a. click the blue "Download .KMZ" at right of the menu bar, and save the .kmz file to your local disk.
      Then open this .kmz file on your machine with google earth to see the photos.
      If you want to share the .kmz file with your friends, you can send them the .kmz file.
   b. click the green "Save the Site" to save this .kmz file on our server. To do so, you need:
      i. click "Login/Register" a) register yourself (your only need to this once) b) login into your account.
      ii. On the pop-up diaglog window, type in the filename you want to save, and click the green "Save .KMZ".
      iii. when it is saved (uploaded to our server), you can click the blue "Copy Link" and share the link with your friends.
           you can download the .kmz file to your local machine by click "Download hosted .KMZ" button.
           
 Now you can share the link with your friends and they can see it directly from our site.
 Open this link: https://photoonmaps.com/?kmz=trip%2Fhuangwei5934-a0fdcd%2Fsanitas-20261121-3%2Fsanitas-20261121-3.kmz
 you will see exactly what we see at our website example page.
 
 
 
